[Music]  in this video I'm gonna teach you how to  thrive in social situations we all have  those situations the certain situations  where we feel totally triggered by  certain people whether that be in work  or out of the pub or at a party wherever  it is there are certain people that  really know how to push our buttons when  we go into these situations the first  thing we want to do is close down and  run away or drink five wines and open up  and do something that we might regret in  the morning what if I told you that the  certain people that trigger you are  giving you an opportunity to grow in  some way what if these people provided  ideal situations for you to move on and  move through your anxiety or your  discomfort or your frustration or anger  or whatever emotions are coming up to  the surface in that moment I'd like to  teach you a tool that really helped me  and thousands of clients that I've  worked with over the years before you go  into a certain situation take a moment  close your eyes and visualize a seat in  front of you and imagine it inviting the  person that triggers you the most and  you may have a hit list here the person  that triggers you the most to come in  and sit on the seat in front of you  while this is happening observe what  kind of feelings and emotions and  tension and tightness start to arise up  in your body and sit with whatever is  coming up so you're visualizing a  situation that's going to happen ahead  of time with the person that triggers  you the most sitting opposite you and  you're witnessing the feelings and  emotions that come up  to the surface all these feelings and  emotions need to be experienced felt or  processed in some way so sit there for a  couple of minutes while everything's  coming up to the surface and breathe  into it after a couple of moments  guaranteed you will feel calmer more  connected to that person and less  stressed about seeing them in that  particular situation that you go to  another tool that helps me really well  in these situations is when I am walking  into a big social group that maybe I'm  meeting for the first time I start to be  aware of the thoughts that are telling  me to close down and run away and I  choose instead to do the very opposite I  choose to open myself up and walk  further into the crowd does that sound  crazy actually what happens is the very  opposite that you are afraid of  happening you are afraid of something  happening in that social situation that  might put you in a place of  vulnerability in some way actually what  happens when you open yourself up and  walk further into the crowd is that they  welcome you with open arms I look  forward to teaching you much more in the  following videos

